/-!
# BuiData3: the exported RD=3 king Bui certificate

The 5930-type king convolution system at split window RD = 3 and its exact
rational super-solution at x = 107350/1000000, giving the conditional bound
`lambda <= 20000/2147` = 9.315324 (see `Upper/BuiRD3.lean`).

Machine-generated by `scripts/gen_bui_cert.lean.py --rd 3` from the system of
`experiments/king_bui.py` / `experiments/king_certificate.py` (canonical 'll'
casing, eps = 1e-3, repair converged after 156 sweeps); cross-checked
against `python3 -m experiments.king_certificate 3` (same x, exact-check PASS).
Do not edit by hand; regenerate instead.

`buiRD3_valid` is the *entire arithmetic side* of the certificate: index
bounds, rank descent, and the cleared-denominator super-solution inequalities,
checked by `native_decide`.  The combinatorial side stays a named hypothesis
(`KingBuiSystemRD3Holds`).
-/

